# @vbcdx/dev-agents — literal configuration template.
#
# This file is READ LITERALLY. It is never sourced, executed, or interpolated:
# a $VAR, a ~, or a `$(...)` stays literal. The operator fills in final values
# here; sourcing a shell beforehand does not expand anything in this file.
#
# Grammar: blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is `#`
# are ignored. An assignment splits at the first `=`; surrounding whitespace is
# trimmed. Unquoted values keep interior spaces, `#`, `=`, and `$` literally.
# Single-quoted values are literal; double-quoted values use JSON escaping.
# All paths are absolute. Duplicate keys (including case-equivalent) are errors.

# ── Required installer directories ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Installer state and the installation manifest root.
VBCDX_AGENTS_BASE_DIR=/home/example/.local/state/vbcdx-agents
# Root under which per-role credential files are written (0700). Need not exist
# when no credential files are needed.
VBCDX_AGENTS_CREDENTIALS_DIR=/home/example/.config/vbcdx/credentials

# ── Selected harness root (only the one you install into is required) ────────
# Required for DSH, and for user scope of the matching harness. Project scope
# uses the containing Git worktree instead. These installer keys are translated
# to the harness's own launch environment variables for user scope
# (VBCDX_AGENTS_DSH_HOME -> DSH_HOME, and so on).
# VBCDX_AGENTS_DSH_HOME=/home/example/.dsh
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/example/.config/claude
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CODEX_HOME=/home/example/.codex
# VBCDX_AGENTS_OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/example/.config/opencode
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_HOME=/home/example/.hermes

# ── Hermes model routing (hermes harness only; nonsecret; optional) ──────────
# Hermes profiles cannot run without a model section. With both set, every
# profile gets a named custom provider whose key is read by Hermes from the
# profile's own .env as HERMES_PROVIDER_API_KEY (never from this file).
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_BASE_URL=https://llm.example/v1
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_MODEL=provider/model-name
# Optional per-role override (suffix as for credentials):
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_MODEL_CODE_AGENT=provider/coder-model

# ── Optional context and integrations ───────────────────────────────────────
# Informational only; never applied to any server configuration.
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CODE_HOST_URL=https://git.example.com
# Absolute path to the nonsecret integrations JSON (see README). Omit for a
# credential-free, no-remote-bindings install.
# VBCDX_AGENTS_INTEGRATIONS_FILE=/home/example/.config/vbcdx/integrations.json

# ── Reserved ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VBCDX_AGENTS_WORKDIR is reserved and unsupported when nonblank; leave it out.

# ── A2A cards server runtime (issue #5; bin/a2a-server.js) ────────────────────
# Runtime configuration for the standalone A2A cards HTTP server. These are read
# from the process environment by that server only; the installer ignores them.
# All are optional and non-secret — the server publishes public cards and needs
# no credentials. Set PUBLIC_BASE_URL on the deployment so the absolute HTTPS
# card URLs are correct; when unset it is derived per request from the Host
# header. PORT defaults to 8080 and HOST to 0.0.0.0.
# PORT=8080
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://agents.example

# ── Optional per-role credentials (USER/TOKEN/PASSWORD per suffix) ───────────
# Installing agents WITHOUT any credentials is fully supported: leave every
# triple blank/absent. For an enabled role, set USER and at least one of
# TOKEN/PASSWORD; leaving all three blank disables that role's remote access.
# The role suffix is the canonical ID uppercased with hyphens as underscores
# (e.g. code-agent -> CODE_AGENT). Note this is CODE_AGENT, not CODER_AGENT.
#
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_ALL_IN_ONE_DEV_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_ALL_IN_ONE_DEV_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_ALL_IN_ONE_DEV_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_CODE_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_CODE_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_CODE_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_COPYWRITER_CONTENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_COPYWRITER_CONTENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_COPYWRITER_CONTENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_COPYWRITER_MARKETING=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_COPYWRITER_MARKETING=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_COPYWRITER_MARKETING=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_CRAZY_IVAN=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_CRAZY_IVAN=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_CRAZY_IVAN=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_DEVOPS_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_DEVOPS_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_DEVOPS_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_INSTRUCTIONAL_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_INSTRUCTIONAL_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_INSTRUCTIONAL_DESIGNER_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_MARKET_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_MARKET_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_MARKET_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_PM_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_PM_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_PM_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_QA_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_QA_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_QA_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_REVIEW_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_REVIEW_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_REVIEW_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_REWARD_HACK_AUDITOR_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_REWARD_HACK_AUDITOR_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_REWARD_HACK_AUDITOR_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_SECURITY_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_SECURITY_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_SECURITY_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_USER_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_USER_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_USER_RESEARCH_AGENT=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_VIDEO_CREATOR=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_VIDEO_CREATOR=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_PASSWORD_VIDEO_CREATOR=
